# Both interface numbers confirmed in-game via:
#   /run print(select(4, GetBuildInfo()))
# 11509 = Classic Era (1.15.9), 16001 = WoW Forever (1.60.1).
# (AtlasLoot Forever's filenames use 11601, but that's their own naming
# convention -- the client itself reports 16001.)
## Interface: 11509, 16001
## Title: ForeverQoL
## Notes: Quality-of-life automation for WoW Forever -- auto repair, junk selling, mail, quests, invites and more. Modular, everything toggleable.
## Author: Spacechicken
## Version: 1.2.0
## SavedVariables: ForeverQoLDB

# Core must load first (it defines the module registry), UI must load last
# (it builds the settings panel from whatever registered in between).
Core.lua

Modules\Vendor.lua
Modules\Mail.lua
Modules\Quests.lua
Modules\Social.lua
Modules\Loot.lua
Modules\Convenience.lua
Modules\Chat.lua
Modules\Tooltips.lua
Modules\Frames.lua

Report.lua

UI.lua
